1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:02,010
If your dog ever smiles

2
00:00:02,030 --> 00:00:04,250
at you with human teeth...

3
00:00:04,270 --> 00:00:06,020
do not smile back.

4
00:00:06,470 --> 00:00:08,480
Do not smile back.

5
00:00:08,550 --> 00:00:10,920
Do not let it eat from your plate.

6
00:00:10,950 --> 00:00:13,230
And never let it look in the mirror.

7
00:00:13,680 --> 00:00:16,410
This is Protocol 404.

8
00:00:16,860 --> 00:00:18,680
There are four rules.

9
00:00:18,700 --> 00:00:20,520
Follow them exactly.

10
00:00:20,540 --> 00:00:21,880
Otherwise, you will have

11
00:00:21,900 --> 00:00:24,000
to activate the emergency protocol.

12
00:00:24,750 --> 00:00:26,120
Rule one.

13
00:00:26,190 --> 00:00:27,960
Do not smile back.

14
00:00:28,410 --> 00:00:29,540
You come home.

15
00:00:29,770 --> 00:00:32,630
Your dog runs to the door, like always.

16
00:00:32,650 --> 00:00:33,670
Tail going.

17
00:00:33,690 --> 00:00:34,670
Ears back.

18
00:00:35,120 --> 00:00:36,810
Then it smiles at you.

19
00:00:37,200 --> 00:00:38,860
Not a dog smile.

20
00:00:38,880 --> 00:00:40,330
A wide one.

21
00:00:40,400 --> 00:00:41,900
And behind its lips,

22
00:00:41,920 --> 00:00:45,390
there is a row of flat, white, human teeth.

23
00:00:46,440 --> 00:00:48,850
Something has moved into your dog.

24
00:00:49,240 --> 00:00:50,460
It learns by copying

25
00:00:50,480 --> 00:00:52,290
the face it sees most.

26
00:00:52,600 --> 00:00:53,610
Yours.

27
00:00:53,640 --> 00:00:56,170
And that smile is not for you.

28
00:00:56,200 --> 00:00:57,330
It is a question.

29
00:00:57,780 --> 00:00:59,120
It is asking if you

30
00:00:59,140 --> 00:01:01,080
are ready to trade places.

31
00:01:01,530 --> 00:01:03,820
You will want to smile back.

32
00:01:03,850 --> 00:01:04,790
You have smiled at your

33
00:01:04,810 --> 00:01:06,900
dog every day of its life.

34
00:01:07,290 --> 00:01:08,740
Do not do it.

35
00:01:08,970 --> 00:01:10,860
A smile is a yes.

36
00:01:11,310 --> 00:01:12,920
Keep your face still.

37
00:01:13,310 --> 00:01:14,360
Pet it.

38
00:01:14,430 --> 00:01:15,800
Say its name.

39
00:01:15,870 --> 00:01:17,320
Then walk away.

40
00:01:17,770 --> 00:01:19,620
One owner smiled back.

41
00:01:19,930 --> 00:01:22,310
His dog stood up on its back legs,

42
00:01:22,330 --> 00:01:24,740
reached out, and patted him on the head.

43
00:01:25,050 --> 00:01:27,060
"Good boy," it said.

44
00:01:27,370 --> 00:01:28,520
In his voice.

45
00:01:29,870 --> 00:01:31,000
Rule two.

46
00:01:31,310 --> 00:01:33,560
Do not let it eat from your plate.

47
00:01:34,010 --> 00:01:35,060
Dinner time.

48
00:01:35,370 --> 00:01:37,580
It does not go to its bowl.

49
00:01:37,610 --> 00:01:39,510
It sits next to your chair.

50
00:01:39,530 --> 00:01:41,120
And watches your fork.

51
00:01:41,570 --> 00:01:43,420
A real dog begs.

52
00:01:43,650 --> 00:01:45,860
This one is studying.

53
00:01:46,050 --> 00:01:47,580
How you hold the fork.

54
00:01:47,890 --> 00:01:49,020
How you chew.

55
00:01:49,330 --> 00:01:51,570
How long you wait between bites.

56
00:01:52,020 --> 00:01:54,000
Do not give it a piece.

57
00:01:54,020 --> 00:01:55,670
Not even one.

58
00:01:55,860 --> 00:01:57,840
Every bite of your food teaches

59
00:01:57,860 --> 00:01:59,310
it what you are made of.

60
00:01:59,760 --> 00:02:02,020
If you do, the next night,

61
00:02:02,040 --> 00:02:04,010
its bowl is still full.

62
00:02:04,080 --> 00:02:05,260
And the chair across from

63
00:02:05,280 --> 00:02:06,730
you has been pulled out.

64
00:02:07,580 --> 00:02:08,950
It is sitting in it.

65
00:02:09,260 --> 00:02:10,230
Back straight.

66
00:02:10,460 --> 00:02:11,950
Paws on the table.

67
00:02:11,980 --> 00:02:13,910
Waiting for you to pass the salt.

68
00:02:14,960 --> 00:02:16,700
Feed it in another room.

69
00:02:16,720 --> 00:02:17,980
Close the door.

70
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:19,060
Eat fast.

71
00:02:19,510 --> 00:02:21,040
Rule three.

72
00:02:21,190 --> 00:02:23,190
Never let it look in the mirror.

73
00:02:23,640 --> 00:02:26,370
Dogs do not care about mirrors.

74
00:02:26,440 --> 00:02:27,620
Yours stops in front

75
00:02:27,640 --> 00:02:29,140
of the hallway mirror.

76
00:02:29,160 --> 00:02:30,430
And stays there.

77
00:02:30,880 --> 00:02:32,770
It is checking its work.

78
00:02:32,800 --> 00:02:35,130
Comparing its teeth to yours.

79
00:02:35,580 --> 00:02:37,510
Do not let it finish looking.

80
00:02:37,660 --> 00:02:38,680
Cover the mirror.

81
00:02:38,700 --> 00:02:39,400
Move it.

82
00:02:39,420 --> 00:02:40,560
Turn it to the wall.

83
00:02:41,010 --> 00:02:44,270
Because the day it sees a face that matches yours,

84
00:02:44,290 --> 00:02:45,930
it stops being a dog.

85
00:02:46,380 --> 00:02:49,000
In the mirror, where your dog is sitting,

86
00:02:49,020 --> 00:02:50,430
there is a person.

87
00:02:50,460 --> 00:02:52,030
On all fours.

88
00:02:52,060 --> 00:02:52,860
Smiling.

89
00:02:53,910 --> 00:02:55,840
And it turns around.

90
00:02:55,990 --> 00:02:57,200
Slowly.

91
00:02:57,270 --> 00:03:00,000
To find out which one of you is the copy.

92
00:03:01,350 --> 00:03:02,760
Rule four.

93
00:03:02,790 --> 00:03:04,600
Emergency protocol.

94
00:03:04,630 --> 00:03:05,910
How to fight back.

95
00:03:06,360 --> 00:03:09,740
If you already smiled back, fed it from your plate,

96
00:03:09,760 --> 00:03:12,970
or let it see the mirror, the trade begins.

97
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:15,590
And if you leave it alone, it finishes.

98
00:03:16,040 --> 00:03:17,170
Three A.M.

99
00:03:17,800 --> 00:03:19,330
You wake up on the floor.

100
00:03:19,640 --> 00:03:21,090
In the dog bed.

101
00:03:21,160 --> 00:03:23,860
Up on your bed, under your blanket,

102
00:03:23,880 --> 00:03:25,930
something is sleeping on your pillow.

103
00:03:26,780 --> 00:03:29,630
And on the nightstand, there is a collar.

104
00:03:29,660 --> 00:03:31,190
With a name tag.

105
00:03:31,260 --> 00:03:32,030
Your name.

106
00:03:32,880 --> 00:03:35,000
Here is what does not work.

107
00:03:35,450 --> 00:03:36,660
Calling the vet.

108
00:03:37,050 --> 00:03:39,060
"His teeth are perfectly healthy.

109
00:03:39,210 --> 00:03:40,600
Healthier than yours."

110
00:03:41,050 --> 00:03:42,820
Locking it outside.

111
00:03:43,290 --> 00:03:46,010
Thirty seconds later, the doorbell rings.

112
00:03:46,460 --> 00:03:47,350
Hiding.

113
00:03:47,820 --> 00:03:49,270
It is still a dog.

114
00:03:49,500 --> 00:03:51,960
It can smell you anywhere in the house.

115
00:03:52,410 --> 00:03:53,590
Fighting it.

116
00:03:53,610 --> 00:03:55,660
Do not even try.

117
00:03:55,690 --> 00:03:57,670
It has the body of a forty-kilo

118
00:03:57,690 --> 00:04:00,580
dog and the mind of a grown man.

119
00:04:00,730 --> 00:04:02,443
Before your hand comes down,

120
00:04:02,463 --> 00:04:04,580
it is already on your chest.

121
00:04:04,650 --> 00:04:06,150
Its human teeth stop

122
00:04:06,170 --> 00:04:08,220
one inch from your throat.

123
00:04:08,330 --> 00:04:09,720
And it smiles.

124
00:04:10,970 --> 00:04:13,540
There is only one thing that works.

125
00:04:13,610 --> 00:04:15,940
Remember how it learned to be you.

126
00:04:16,250 --> 00:04:17,430
It copies you.

127
00:04:17,880 --> 00:04:20,050
So give it something else to copy.

128
00:04:20,360 --> 00:04:21,520
Be the dog.

129
00:04:21,970 --> 00:04:23,870
Get down on all fours.

130
00:04:23,890 --> 00:04:25,460
Pull your lips back.

131
00:04:25,490 --> 00:04:26,910
Show your teeth.

132
00:04:26,930 --> 00:04:28,340
And growl.

133
00:04:28,370 --> 00:04:29,380
Loud.

134
00:04:29,410 --> 00:04:31,500
Louder than it has ever heard you.

135
00:04:32,550 --> 00:04:33,760
It hesitates.

136
00:04:34,070 --> 00:04:36,360
It has never seen you do this.

137
00:04:36,550 --> 00:04:39,160
Then it does what it always does.

138
00:04:39,190 --> 00:04:40,340
It copies you.

139
00:04:40,790 --> 00:04:42,850
It drops to four legs.

140
00:04:42,870 --> 00:04:44,760
Its lips pull back.

141
00:04:44,790 --> 00:04:46,840
It growls back at you.

142
00:04:46,870 --> 00:04:48,890
And the more it copies a dog,

143
00:04:48,910 --> 00:04:50,690
the less room there is for you.

144
00:04:51,740 --> 00:04:54,950
One by one, the human teeth fall out.

145
00:04:55,260 --> 00:04:55,990
Click.

146
00:04:56,220 --> 00:04:57,080
Click.

147
00:04:57,100 --> 00:04:57,830
Click.

148
00:04:58,060 --> 00:04:59,630
Onto the floor.

149
00:04:59,820 --> 00:05:02,100
Sharp dog teeth slide back in.

150
00:05:03,350 --> 00:05:03,490
Bark.

151
00:05:03,510 --> 00:05:04,930
It barks.

152
00:05:04,950 --> 00:05:07,730
Scratch behind your ear.

153
00:05:07,750 --> 00:05:09,890
It scratches behind its ear.

154
00:05:09,910 --> 00:05:11,440
Do not stop until the

155
00:05:11,510 --> 00:05:13,490
last human tooth hits the floor.

156
00:05:14,340 --> 00:05:15,920
Then ask the question only

157
00:05:15,940 --> 00:05:18,110
a real dog cannot answer.

158
00:05:18,500 --> 00:05:20,210
"Who's a good boy?"

159
00:05:20,660 --> 00:05:22,830
It does not say "I am."

160
00:05:23,060 --> 00:05:24,620
It just wags its tail.

161
00:05:25,670 --> 00:05:26,690
In the morning,

162
00:05:26,710 --> 00:05:28,960
your dog is asleep in its bed.

163
00:05:29,030 --> 00:05:30,210
Normal teeth.

164
00:05:30,230 --> 00:05:31,190
Normal dog.

165
00:05:31,640 --> 00:05:33,530
You go to brush your teeth.

166
00:05:33,560 --> 00:05:35,120
You smile at the mirror.

167
00:05:35,570 --> 00:05:36,820
Top row.

168
00:05:36,850 --> 00:05:38,060
Left side.

169
00:05:38,130 --> 00:05:39,950
One of your teeth is long,

170
00:05:39,970 --> 00:05:42,400
and sharp, and not yours.

171
00:05:43,650 --> 00:05:44,940
It copied you.

172
00:05:45,250 --> 00:05:47,750
And for a few minutes last night...

173
00:05:47,770 --> 00:05:48,980
you copied it.

174
00:05:49,830 --> 00:05:52,720
And that was Protocol 404.

175
00:05:53,170 --> 00:05:55,790
If this ever happens to you...

176
00:05:55,810 --> 00:05:57,110
you know the protocol.
